  <h2>Why Get an eSIM for Korea?</h2>
  <p>South Korea has some of the <strong>fastest 5G networks in the world</strong>. The moment you land at Incheon Airport, you'll need internet for navigation, translation, booking, and staying connected. An eSIM is the smartest way to do it — no SIM card swapping, no airport queues.</p>

  <h2>What is an eSIM?</h2>
  <p>An eSIM (embedded SIM) is a digital SIM card built into your phone. You scan a QR code and activate a data plan instantly — done. You can buy and set it up at home before your flight.</p>

  <div class="tip-box">
    💡 <strong>Check compatibility first:</strong> iPhone XS or later, Samsung Galaxy S20 or later, Google Pixel 3 or later. Some carrier-locked phones may not support eSIM — check with your carrier.
  </div>

